The objective of this report is to provide summaries and treatment group
comparisons of the pen-level and individual data for TRL000411, an *A.
oryzae* fermentation product IVP nursery study conducted at GBI in Fergus
Falls, MN.

<br>

The experimental design consisted of 4 treatment groups. One strict
negative control group received no F18 challenge and was housed
separately for biosecurity reasons. The remaining three groups received
an F18 E. coli challenge: the positive control, the low-dose IVP group
(1BP, BP-L), and the high-dose IVP group (2BP, BP-SL). The main
comparison of interest is to assess whether the IVP treatments reduce
the negative impact of the F18 challenge on clinical outcomes and
performance relative to the challenged positive control. No statistical
comparisons were made between the two IVP treatment groups.

