corresponds to a pen within a treatment and trial period, with the
associated body weight, average pig weight, feed intake, and removal
information. These data were then used to calculate BWG, FCR, GF,
ADFI, and ADG for the statistical analysis.

Note on FCR interpretation during the challenge phase: **FCR can be
negative when pigs lose weight** (i.e. when the denominator BWG < 0). In a
controlled F18 challenge model this is an expected and biologically
meaningful outcome — it reflects the severity of the acute response, not
a data error. Negative FCR values are reported and should be interpreted
as indicating net weight loss during that period. The GF column provides
a complementary metric with consistent directionality.

