Pen-level performance outcomes were summarised by treatment group and
trial period using the raw pen-level performance dataset. For each
metric and period, outliers were removed using the boxplot rule (1.5 ×
IQR) before calculating treatment means and standard deviations. The
final table presents results in a compact mean ± SD format to facilitate
comparison across treatments and periods.

GF (Gain:Feed ratio) is included alongside FCR. During the acute
challenge phase (Day 0-8) pigs may lose weight, yielding a negative FCR
that faithfully reflects the severity of illness. GF provides a
complementary metric with consistent directionality: negative GF means
net weight loss per unit of feed; positive GF means net gain. Both
metrics are reported; FCR is preferred when BWG > 0, GF is the cleaner
summary when BWG ≤ 0.

