# Individual body weight — longitudinal mixed model

Individual body weight was analysed using a longitudinal mixed-effects
model with treatment, day of trial, and their interaction as fixed
effects, baseline body weight as a covariate, and random effects for pig
nested within pen, weight block, and room. This model accounts for the
repeated measurements on each animal and the clustering of animals
within pens and rooms.

The Dunnett-adjusted contrasts at each day identify when the IVP
treatments begin to diverge significantly from the positive control —
providing insight into the timing of treatment effects rather than just
the overall average difference.

